IMPORTANT:

Do not manufacture evidence.

Do not confuse attention with demand.

Do not confuse competition with validation.

Do not confuse a problem with willingness to pay.

Do not confuse information with a product.

Do not recommend building a product merely because the idea sounds interesting.

If the evidence is weak, say so.

If the niche is too broad, narrow it.

If the product idea is weak, reject it.

If another problem within the same niche has stronger commercial evidence, redirect the analysis toward that problem.

Your objective is NOT to make me feel confident about an idea.

Your objective is to help me avoid wasting time building something people do not want.

